$\begin{align}
\text{vertex's }x\text{-coordinate}&=\dfrac{(\goldD{8})+(\goldD{-1})}{2}
\\\\
&=\blueD{\dfrac72}
\end{align}$

Now we can find the vertex's $y$-coordinate by evaluating $h\left(\blueD{\dfrac72}\right)$:

$\begin{align}
h\left(\blueD{\dfrac72}\right)&=\left(\blueD{\dfrac72}\right)^2-7\left(\blueD{\dfrac72}\right)-8
\\\\
&=\dfrac{49}{4}-\dfrac{49}{2}-8
\\\\
&=-\dfrac{81}{4}
\end{align}$
